  "findings": [
    "ESP-IDF efuse S3 esp_efuse_rtc_calib_get_ver accepts BLK_VERSION_MAJOR exactly1; all other values return0 with the actual warning seen in039.",
    "The S3 eFuse table places BLK_VERSION_MAJOR at BLOCK2 bit128 width2. Calibration version1 is the only accepted curve-fitting version.",
    "The upstream S3 QEMU model inherits esp_efuse.c, not the older esp32_efuse.c. Without a supplied drive it allocates a zero-filled volatile mirror. Original039 has no eFuse drive.",
    "adc_cali_create_scheme_curve_fitting rejects version0 before allocating a calibration handle. Archived ESP-Miner ADC_get_vcore then gets a real calibration error and returns0; it does not measure the supplied voltage successfully.",
    "ADC1 attenuation3 init-code decoding uses four eFuse differences plus1850+90+70. Calibration reference digit for attenuation3 is its eight-bit difference plus900 at850mV. These fields are coupled to real silicon factory measurements.",
    "Curve conversion uses the exact first-stage integer coefficient and selected manufacturer second-stage polynomial. Supplying a version bit alone would not establish calibrated analog behavior.",
    "The acquired adc_ll digi power function sets APB digital xpd_sar_force=3 for ON and2 for OFF. This is not by itself the RTC SENS field contract. The prior RTC/TRM conflict remains visible."
  ],
  "not_implemented": [
    "No guessed trim, version bit, voltage reply or calibration success was inserted.",
    "No eFuse image, ADC model change, original040 rerun or physical calibration claim."
  ],
  "next_action": "Define a separate reference eFuse/ADC transfer fixture with explicit provenance and independent conversion vectors, then test actual firmware calibration. Exact physical targets still require their own factory data or an evidenced compatible policy.",
